  "notes": "Two of the research's phrases are the same parameter seen from either side — \"spacious mix with the loop given room\" and \"low instrumental note density behind the vocal\" — and together they produce the sparsest melody in this batch: `densityPerBar` [1,4], two perc lanes at [0,1], `velocityTiers.main` down to 72–86, and `hihat.fillDensity` 0.4. What fills the space is a single sustained phrase, so `articulation` is legato and `contour.descend` leads. Ayatollah's documented habit of keeping the sample's vocals and writing around them is why `timbreHint` is `chopped_vocal` and why the harmony is left simple: i–iv and i–VI–VII over 2–4 bar loops, with a bare-`i` family at weight 2 for the loops where the sustained phrase is the whole event. ⚠ The bass is `independent_riff` at a middling `followRootsProb` of 0.68 because the research describes two cases at once — sample-internal bass plus modest sub on the loop cuts, real electric with genuine changes on the live cuts — and 0.68 is the honest midpoint rather than a reading of either. That is the INFERRED parameter in this file. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high: the defining beat's construction is documented first-person, but the drum numbers and tempo band are not. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 46 to 45 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 46 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 1.",
